## Summary

The error handler is "not found" when the serializer fails, resulting in a fatal error instead of graceful failure.

## Description
Looking at `plumber::serializer_json`, it looks like serializers take an `errorHandler` as the last argument.

```R
# plumber::serializer_json
function (...) 
{
    function(val, req, res, errorHandler) {
        tryCatch({
            json <- jsonlite::toJSON(val, ...)
            res$setHeader("Content-Type", "application/json")
            res$body <- json
            return(res$toResponse())
        }, error = function(e) {
            errorHandler(req, res, e)
        })
    }
}
```

I have implemented several custom serializers with the same `tryCatch` structure and I have noticed that errors are not properly caught because the catching code fails with `object 'errorHandler' not found`.

## To reproduce

It is easy to reproduce with the basic json serializer:

```r
# plumber.R

#* @get /error
#* @serializer json
function() {
  # Something that cannot be serialized as a json
  lm(mpg ~ ., data = mtcars)
}
```

This fails with the error: `<simpleError in ser(value, req, res, errorHandler): object 'errorHandler' not found>`

The response only contains `An exception occurred.`

My `plumber.R` file:
```r
#* @post /test
function(req,res,param){
    print(req$postBody)
    if(!jsonlite::validate(req$postBody)){
        res$status <- 415
        return(list(errors="message body is not JSON, or not properly formatted JSON!"))
    }
}
```
Once the API is live (`library(plumber);r <- plumb("plumber.R");r$run(port=8000)`), executing `curl --data '{"param":123}'` returns the error message. However, in a R console, `validate('{"param":123}')` evaluates to TRUE.

The `print()` statement returns `"'{param:123}'"` (notice how the `""` have been removed from around `param`), which explains why the error is raised, as `req$postBody` is not proper JSON anymore. **How to access the raw, original quoted JSON with req$postBody?**

Any help would be much appreciated, thank you!

